    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d769">

                <pb facs="0897" n="801" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg801"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">361.11/3796: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commissioner at Riga</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Young</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Riga</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-08-18T13:00:00+01:36"><hi rendition="#italic">August 18,
                                1921—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 2:09 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>490. <hi rendition="#italic">Izvestia</hi> August 12 carries prominent notice
                    official information Chicherin to effect American citizens may leave Russia
                    after presenting satisfactory proof citizenship to Anglo-American Division
                    Commission Foreign Affairs. Keeley<anchor n="10" xml:id="d769-f1"/> telegraphs
                    expects to leave within a few days.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Young</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d769-f1" n="10" xml:id="d769-f1-content">
                <p>Royal R. Keeley, who entered Russia in September 1919 to work for the Soviet
                    Government, was arrested in May 1920 and imprisoned on the charge of sending out
                    a false report on economic conditions.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
